{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/7/codegen_prompts/8.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1692361792/7`\n- 题号：`8`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1692361792/7/8.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"8\">\n- `description`：将网格中的彩色对象按其所在象限分组，然后将同一象限内的所有对象合并为一个复合图案，绘制到对应象限的固定锚点位置。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为Black。\n  - 网格中央有一条Red水平线和一条Red垂直线交叉形成十字，将网格分为四个象限。\n  - 四个象限中各散布着1到3个不同颜色的小型4-连通对象（每个对象bbox不超过3x3），同一象限内的对象颜色互不相同。\n  - 每个象限的角落（远离十字交叉点的角）有一个Yellow单像素标记作为锚点。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个象限，收集其中所有的小型彩色对象。\n  - 计算每个对象相对于该象限十字交叉点角的偏移量（即对象中心相对于交叉点的行偏移和列偏移）。\n  - 将这些对象以相同的相对位置关系叠加在一起，形成一个复合图案。当不同颜色的像素重叠时，保留两种颜色（实际上由于对象较小且位置不同，极少重叠）。\n  - 将复合图案平移到该象限的Yellow锚点位置，使复合图案的bbox角与锚点对齐（锚点位于象限外角，图案向十字方向展开）。\n  - 清除所有对象的原始位置。Red十字线和Yellow锚点保持不变。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现十字线将空间分为四个象限且对象按象限分组，再发现每个象限内的对象需要被\"收拢\"到角落锚点处并保持相对位置——分组的空间逻辑和保持相对位置的合并逻辑构成两层推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/5ecac7f7, train/9f669b64, train/20fb2937, train/e39e9282, train/689c358e, train/2faf500b, train/c6141b15, train/84551f4c\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5ecac7f7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3676\nmechanism=0.4484\nlexical=0.0135\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:line_segment, object:sprite, operation:translate, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5ecac7f7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5ecac7f7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nCombine the left, middle, and right ordered objects from three separated panels.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is three HxH panels separated by one-cell vertical separator bars.\n- The background is the dominant color, and each panel contains exactly three same-color 4-connected foreground objects.\n\nRule\n- Build a new HxH background canvas.\n- From the left panel copy its leftmost object, from the middle panel copy its middle object, and from the right panel copy its rightmost object.\n\nKey insight\n- The separator bars create three aligned layers, and the panel's own left-to-right object order selects which object survives in the merged output.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"three divider-separated square panels, each with three 4-connected same-color objects ordered left-to-right\",\n  \"dst\": \"compose the selected objects onto one square output canvas at their original panel coordinates\",\n  \"transform\": \"copy object 1 from panel 1, object 2 from panel 2, and object 3 from panel 3; discard the other objects and separator columns\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"3 HxH panels with two separator columns -> HxH output\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9f669b64\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3444\nmechanism=0.4322\nlexical=0.0127\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:line_segment, object:sprite, operation:translate, output:same_size, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/9f669b64.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9f669b64.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPush the central solid rectangle to the grid edge, splitting the perpendicular target rectangle around its path.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly three monochrome foreground objects arranged on one\n  horizontal or vertical axis.\n- The middle object on that axis is a solid rectangular moving object.\n- One end object is a solid rectangle or bar whose long side is perpendicular\n  to the movement axis; this is the target to split.\n\nRule\n- Move the middle rectangle along the axis toward the target until it is\n  flush with the grid edge in that direction.\n- Clear the original middle rectangle and the original target.\n- Split the target through the moving rectangle's two-cell-wide path and\n  shift the two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement.\n- Keep the other end object unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The non-target end object acts as a pusher; the central rectangle travels\n  away from it through the perpendicular target, opening a matching gap.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"middle solid rectangular object between two end objects\",\n  \"path\": \"straight horizontal or vertical line away from the non-target end object and through the perpendicular solid target rectangle/bar\",\n  \"dst\": \"place flush with the grid edge beyond the target\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint only the final moved rectangle at dst\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase original source pixels; split the target rectangle/bar along the moving object's two-cell-wide path and shift its two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement; keep the other end object unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"20fb2937\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3477\nmechanism=0.4368\nlexical=0.0134\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:axis, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:translate, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/20fb2937.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/20fb2937.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nReplace each marker below the separator with the mapped top legend square centered on that marker.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background surrounds a top legend, one solid non-background separator row, and a lower marker field.\n- The legend contains equal-size filled square sprites, with a singleton marker below each sprite and aligned to its center column.\n- The lower field contains only background and marker colors from the legend.\n\nRule:\n- Pair legend markers to legend sprites by left-to-right position.\n- Discard the legend and separator; keep the grid width and the rows below the separator.\n- In the lower field, replace every marker pixel by a filled square of the paired sprite color, centered at the marker location.\n\nKey insight: The top area is a positional color legend, and the actual output is the post-separator marker field expanded by that legend.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"filled square sprite s in the top legend\",\n  \"dst\": \"lower marker d as center anchor\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.color == singleton marker color below s\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"top legend maps each singleton marker color to its filled square sprite\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"rows below the separator, same width\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e39e9282\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3148\nmechanism=0.3700\nlexical=0.0162\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:translate, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e39e9282.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e39e9282.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nProject maroon markers into adjacent grey or pink 3x3 squares, erasing grey squares afterward.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background, solid 3x3 grey and/or pink squares, and maroon marker pixels or segments directly touching one side of exactly one square.\nRule\nGrey squares are erased; their adjacent maroon markers stay in place and stamp the nearest edge cell inside the grey square. Pink squares stay pink; their adjacent maroon markers disappear and stamp the corresponding cell on the square's middle row or middle column.\nKey insight\nThe side touched by a marker determines the projection: grey uses the near edge, while pink uses the centerline, preserving the marker's coordinate along that side.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"maroon marker pixels or segments adjacent to solid grey or pink 3x3 square objects\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase grey squares after stamping maroon into each touched near-edge cell; keep grey-adjacent markers in place; keep pink squares, remove pink-adjacent markers, and stamp their maroon cells onto the matching middle row or column of the pink square\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"689c358e\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3449\nmechanism=0.4584\nlexical=0.0160\ncode_feature=0.2500\noverlap_tags=code:connected_components, object:axis, object:line_segment, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:translate, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/689c358e.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/689c358e.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMark each arrow-like sprite's pointed frame endpoint with its color and the opposite endpoint black.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a one-pixel solid rectangular frame around a dominant interior background.\n- Inside the frame are monochrome six-pixel sprites shaped as asymmetric T arrows.\n- Each sprite has a length-4 bar and a length-3 crossbar one cell closer to the pointed end.\n\nRule:\n- For each sprite, follow its bar axis from the shorter end to the frame.\n- Paint that frame endpoint with the sprite color.\n- Paint the opposite endpoint on the same row or column black.\n- Leave the interior background, sprites, and all other frame pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- The direction is encoded by the crossbar's off-center position: the nearer end is the pointing end.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"monochrome six-pixel asymmetric T sprites inside a solid frame\",\n  \"path\": \"orthogonal ray from each sprite's shorter bar end to the frame, plus the opposite ray on the same row or column\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
